{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01U2ry56et2gAgfVb6428f2F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/01-009-what-is-kv-cache-how-does-it-help-in-llm-inference.md`** — Q9: *What is KV cache? How does it help in LLM inference?*\n\nKey content:\n- **Concept:** KV cache stores past tokens' Key and Value tensors so the decode loop reads from cache instead of recomputing — reduces per-step cost from O(n²) → O(n)\n- **Mechanism:** Prefill phase processes full prompt and populates cache; decode phase computes only the new token's Q/K/V and reads cached K/V. Memory formula included (2 × layers × heads × head_dim × seq_len × bytes)\n- **Example/Tradeoff:** Quantified memory cost (~8 GB for 70B @ 4K tokens), PagedAttention / vLLM 2–4× throughput gain, KV quantization (KVQuant INT4), sliding-window (Mistral)\n- **3 pitfalls:** Not specifying *what* is cached (K+V, not Q), ignoring memory pressure on batch size, conflating TTFT vs inter-token latency\n- **Cross-links:** Q2 (transformers), Q34 (memory-bounded inference), cost/latency category\n\n40 items remain in Next."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":55101,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":342,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c74bc44b-b83e-4535-b6a8-cbd91a8f1626","uuid":"801e2c04-4018-467b-bebf-430956f5ec07"}
